     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum recommended metformin dose.\n\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, depending on formulation and labeling. Immediate-release is typically 2,500 mg/day, split into 2\u20133 doses.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is also well above the usual maximum for one dose, which is about 850\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders are:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided into two or three doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
      }
     ],
